1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,940
 - Hello, I'm Dr. Charles Severance

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:04,720
 from the University of Michigan School of Information.

3
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:08,220
 Welcome to my introductory Python course on Udemy.

4
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:11,140
 This course is designed for people

5
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:12,940
 who want to learn programming,

6
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:15,580
 even if they've never written a line of code.

7
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:18,540
 There is no math and no algebra.

8
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:21,580
 All you need is curiosity and a willingness

9
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:24,720
 to be patient with yourself as you learn.

10
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,700
 I've taught Python to millions of learners around the world,

11
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,900
 and my goal is to explain not only what to type

12
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:35,420
 but why programming works the way that it does.

13
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,660
 These days, artificial intelligence

14
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:40,980
 can make typing code trivial,

15
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,160
 but you still need to understand how programming works

16
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:46,100
 if you want to use AI effectively in software development.

17
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:48,420
 Learning to program is hard,

18
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:51,220
 and I have never forgotten how difficult

19
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:54,540
 and confusing my first programming course was.

20
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:56,340
 This course addresses that difficulty

21
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:59,660
 directly throughout the course and helps you work through it

22
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:02,820
 step by step until you begin to feel

23
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:05,140
 and think like a programmer.

24
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:08,660
 We begin with basic ideas of variables and expressions,

25
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:11,300
 conditional execution, functions, and loops.

26
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:14,520
 Then we move into strings, data structures, and files.

27
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:18,500
 You'll watch short lectures, examine working examples,

28
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:21,340
 and write Python programs yourself.

29
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:24,460
 This course is designed to take you from a complete beginner

30
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:28,220
 to someone who is ready to write simple Python programs,

31
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:32,840
 and more importantly, someone who feels confident enough

32
